# Rust build artifacts.
#
# `target/` is machine-generated, architecture-specific, and enormous — a full workspace
# build here is several gigabytes. Nothing in it belongs in history, and committing it
# would make every clone unusable.
/target/

# The research material.
#
# The dependency research, the process-execution measurements, the raw crates.io responses
# and the probe workspace now live in a repository of their own:
# https://github.com/antstanley/nanus-research (private). They are evidence rather than
# shipped code, and keeping them here made a clone carry scratch material. Ignored rather
# than merely deleted, so a stray copy cannot be re-added by accident.
.research/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local configuration and credentials. A harness reads its key from the environment, but
# a stray local file must never be the thing that publishes one.
.env
*.local.toml

# Node tooling for the docs site.
#
# The docs site (apps/website) is an Astro + Starlight project built and installed
# with pnpm. Dependencies, the Astro-generated types, and the build output are all
# machine-generated and are rebuilt from the lockfile, so they are ignored rather
# than committed. These patterns have no leading slash, so they match at any depth.
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/

# The code-graph index.
#
# `.graph-search/` is the index a `graph-search` build writes into a workspace: a few
# megabytes of machine-generated JSON and binary, derived entirely from the sources it
# indexes and rebuilt by re-running the tool. Nothing in the harness reads it, and it is
# large enough that `jj` refuses to snapshot parts of it. It is ignored rather than merely
# absent, so a future index cannot be committed by accident — the same reason `.research/`
# is listed above, and the role `.codegraph/.gitignore` plays for the other index beside it.
# The pattern has no leading slash, so it matches at any depth.
.graph-search/

# Jujutsu's working state is not tracked; `.jj/` is written by `jj git init` itself and
# is already listed in its own ignore file, so it is named here only for clarity.
/.jj/
